course: dictionary
lesson: 5192
title: Jackrabbit: a hare with a misleading name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A jackrabbit sounds like a rabbit, but it is a hare. Context helps you spot this: «Jackrabbits are hares; hares are bigger than rabbits, with longer ears and legs, and live above ground in nests in grass.» The clues are bigger, longer ears and longer legs, so think hare, not rabbit.
explain: Science lessons about deserts often mention jackrabbits. Their huge ears help them lose heat, which keeps them cool in hot weather. Some can run up to about 60 km per hour, which is very fast for an animal that lives in open, hot land.
explain: The word can also be a verb in American English, but this use is informal. If a car jackrabbits away from the traffic lights, it starts suddenly and moves fast. A «jackrabbit start» is a quick, sudden start like that. When you meet a new meaning, check the sentence: does the word still make sense as the animal, or does it describe speed?
fact: A jackrabbit is a large hare of western North America.
fact: Jackrabbits have very long ears and strong back legs.
fact: Despite the name, a jackrabbit is a hare, not a rabbit.
fact: Hares are born with fur and open eyes.
fact: «Jackrabbit» can also be a verb in informal American English: to start or move suddenly and fast.
exercise: Why do jackrabbits have such huge ears? | To hear songs from birds | To carry food back to the nest | To swim faster | *To lose heat
exercise: Despite its name, what kind of animal is a jackrabbit? | A bird that cannot fly | A kind of fish | A rabbit with a different name | *A hare
exercise: «The car jackrabbited away from the traffic lights.» What does jackrabbited mean here? | Honked loudly | Rolled backwards | Stopped slowly | *Started suddenly and moved fast
test: Some jackrabbits can run up to about how fast? | *About 60 km per hour | About 16 km per hour | About 6 km per hour | About 600 km per hour
test: Hares are born with fur and open eyes. What does this tell you about the difference between hares and rabbits? | Hares are born blind and bald | *Hares are born ready to see and move, unlike many baby rabbits | Hares are born only in winter | Hares and rabbits are born exactly the same
exam: What is a «black-tailed jackrabbit»? | A bird from the desert | A car that starts very fast | A black rabbit with a long tail | *A type of jackrabbit with a black tail
